{"vid":"p3XukomQaGA","source":"p3XukomQaGA.en.json3","lang":"en","cues":[{"t":0.1,"txt":"A lot of Americans are worried about the job market"},{"t":2.2,"txt":"right now, and even billionaires are worried"},{"t":3.8,"txt":"about their kids' futures. I spoke with Patrick Dwyer."},{"t":6.2,"txt":"He works in wealth management and helps"},{"t":7.9,"txt":"billionaire clients handle their money."},{"t":10,"txt":"A lot of Patrick's clients, who have net worths ranging"},{"t":12.5,"txt":"between $100 million and over $1 billion,"},{"t":14.7,"txt":"are growing increasingly concerned that their kids,"},{"t":17.1,"txt":"primarily between the ages of 22 and 35,"},{"t":19.5,"txt":"won't be able to sustain long term careers in even"},{"t":21.9,"txt":"traditionally safe fields like technology,"},{"t":24.7,"txt":"medicine and law."},{"t":25.9,"txt":"That uncertainty is part of a larger trend."},{"t":28.1,"txt":"The unemployment rate for recent college graduates has"},{"t":30.8,"txt":"been growing for the last three years,"},{"t":32.8,"txt":"and 2025 was the weakest year of US job creation"},{"t":35.6,"txt":"since 2009, excluding 2020."},{"t":38.7,"txt":"Some experts are pointing to AI as a major market"},{"t":41.4,"txt":"disruptor. Others are saying that economic factors,"},{"t":44.8,"txt":"like the rising cost of living,"},{"t":46.6,"txt":"is causing people to cling on to their current jobs."},{"t":49.1,"txt":"To be clear, the ultra wealthy aren't necessarily"},{"t":51.8,"txt":"worried about going broke."},{"t":53.1,"txt":"This isn't a major financial strain for many of them."},{"t":56.7,"txt":"What they are concerned about is this kind of"},{"t":58.8,"txt":"economic efficiency, according to Patrick."},{"t":61.6,"txt":"They don't want to pour money and resources and time"},{"t":64.7,"txt":"into their kids training, education or early careers"},{"t":68.3,"txt":"if those careers are eventually going to be"},{"t":69.9,"txt":"plateaued, disrupted, or even replaced by AI."},{"t":73.1,"txt":"Patrick says children from affluent families used to"},{"t":75.4,"txt":"kind of follow the same formula."},{"t":77.1,"txt":"They'd get into prestigious schools,"},{"t":79.1,"txt":"lean on their connections, and then land internships at"},{"t":81.8,"txt":"high profile companies, maybe like Goldman Sachs."},{"t":84.6,"txt":"Then they'd use that training, education,"},{"t":86.5,"txt":"and those connections to work their way up the career"},{"t":88.8,"txt":"ladder. That old career ladder is starting to break."},{"t":92.5,"txt":"The ultra wealthy are becoming increasingly"},{"t":94.4,"txt":"concerned that their children may have to make"},{"t":96.3,"txt":"lifestyle sacrifices if their careers end up not"},{"t":98.7,"txt":"being sustainable long term."},{"t":100.3,"txt":"Now, the ultra wealthy are considering strategies to"},{"t":102.9,"txt":"ensure they can pass down more wealth to their kids."},{"t":105.7,"txt":"They're thinking about retiring later or investing"},{"t":107.9,"txt":"more bullishly to earn money for a little longer."},{"t":111.1,"txt":"They're also pushing their kids to work in startups or"},{"t":113.6,"txt":"launch businesses of their own."},{"t":115.3,"txt":"Entrepreneurship is often considered a low paying,"},{"t":118.3,"txt":"time intensive endeavor, with a high failure rate"},{"t":121.3,"txt":"that can make working in any kind of startup a risky"},{"t":124,"txt":"career proposition for many Americans."},{"t":126.2,"txt":"But it's a high risk, high reward endeavor,"},{"t":128.4,"txt":"Patrick says. The children of ultra wealthy families"},{"t":130.8,"txt":"often have enough capital to experiment."},{"t":133.3,"txt":"They can start and shutter multiple startups before one"},{"t":136.1,"txt":"even starts to turn a profit."},{"t":137.9,"txt":"Ultimately, while billionaires are facing the"},{"t":139.9,"txt":"same uncertain job market as the rest of us,"},{"t":142.8,"txt":"they have more money to gamble when it comes to"},{"t":144.9,"txt":"helping th